-- Copies seerr's rows out of its SQLite file into the postgres-seerr cluster.
-- Read by the Job in job.yaml. {{VARS}} are filled from the Job's environment
-- by pgloader's mustache templating; the password comes from PGPASSWORD, which
-- pgloader honours when the URI carries none, so it is never URL-encoded into
-- a connection string.
--
-- data only: seerr has already created the schema from its own migrations on
-- first start, so pgloader must not create tables or indexes. It still drops
-- the foreign keys for the duration of the copy and recreates them after, which
-- is what makes the load order irrelevant.
-- quote identifiers: typeorm's columns are camelCase and quoted. pgloader's
-- default downcasing would COPY into columns that do not exist.
-- truncate: seerr seeds discover_slider on every start, and those rows carry
-- the same ids as the ones being copied in. It also makes a re-run safe.
-- migrations excluded: the SQLite and PostgreSQL migration histories are
-- different files with different names. The PostgreSQL set is already recorded
-- and copying the SQLite rows over it would make the next start attempt the
-- initial migration again, against tables that exist.
LOAD DATABASE
  FROM sqlite:///app/config/db/db.sqlite3
  INTO postgresql://{{DB_USER}}@{{DB_HOST}}:{{DB_PORT}}/{{DB_NAME}}
  WITH data only, quote identifiers, truncate, reset sequences
  EXCLUDING TABLE NAMES LIKE 'migrations'
;
